WEBVTT

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:02.670
Say, Kazuya.

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:03.850
Yes?

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:03.980
Tsugumomo 3

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:03.980
<b>Hamada Yoshikazu</b>

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:06.730
Hurry and hand me the next one!

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:04.100
Tsugumomo 3

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:04.100
<b>Hamada Yoshikazu</b>

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:04.230
Tsugumomo 3

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:04.230
<b>Hamada Yoshikazu</b>

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.480
Tsugumomo 3

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.480
<b>Hamada Yoshikazu</b>

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:08.540
I'm not done reading it.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:11.110
What? You're awfully slow.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.610
Hey, don't eat in bed!

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:22.580
What's this? Did you order some 
"inspiration" for your self-abuse?

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:23.870
I did no such thing!

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:25.630
Coming.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:31.660
Huh? Sunao-san...

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.360
<b>The mortality of tsukumogami.</b>

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.620
<b>A tsukumogami will return 
to being an inanimate object</b>

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:44.020
Kettle

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.510
<b>if all of its spiritual power is exhausted.</b>

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:44.020
<b>To a tsukumogami, this is 
not dissimilar to death.</b>

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:07.090
<b>Tsugumomo</b>

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.160
<b>Tsugu</b>

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:18.490
m 0 0 l 0 -10 l 10 -10 l 10 0

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:18.490
m 0 0 l 0 -10 l 10 -10 l 10 0

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:18.490
<b>Chapter 5</b>

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:18.490
<b>Sunao and Kotetsu</b>

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:18.490
"Sunao and Kotetsu."

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:21.990
Whaddaya mean Kotetsu ain't wakin' up?

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:23.380
Well...

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:27.750
His hilt was repaired yesterday, and he 
was sent home from the swordsmith,

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:31.000
but I keep calling to him, 
and there's no response.

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:35.250
I had Honoka-sama take 
a look right away, and...

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:39.260
As a tsukumogami, he's not quite dead,

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:41.760
but his spiritual strength 
is just about gone.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:46.520
If he doesn't wake soon, you'll have 
nothing but a regular sword left.

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:49.570
That's terrible! 
Is there anything you can do?

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:52.330
She told me there was one option.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:55.520
An echo stone from the Cave 
of the Divine Navel, huh?

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:57.280
An echo stone?

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:59.770
It's an altar made from stone

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:03.980
that's been bathin' in spirit 
energy for hundreds of years.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:07.120
It's become a kinda spiritual amplifier

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.380
that can even let people 
hear the voices of objects

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:11.340
that ain't become tsukumogami yet.

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:16.210
That oughta let you talk 
to Kotetsu, all right.

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:20.800
Wait, so why didn't you 
head straight there?

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:22.740
Well...

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:27.070
The Cave of the Divine Navel 
is a spiritually unstable spot.

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:29.180
There's no telling what could happen.

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:33.400
Right now, you're just a 
normal human with a sword.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:36.060
It's too great a risk to let you go alone.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:42.160
Since the Divine Navel can amplify 
the voices of even inanimate objects,

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:46.980
someone as powerful as Honoka-sama 
can't go with me, either.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:48.330
I see.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:51.710
Indeed. And that's where we come in, yes?

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:54.830
Very well, then. In that case, 
let's get a move on.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.000
Right now?

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.840
Yes, right now!

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.970
<b>Tawami</b>

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.970
<i>The train arriving on track 14 is...</i>

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.970
<b>Departures</b>

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.970
<b>Tawami</b>

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.970
<b>Scheduled Stops</b>

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.970
<b>Scheduled Stops</b>

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.970
<b>Scheduled Stops</b>

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.970
<b>Tawami</b>

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:02.720
Fast!

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:04.220
Huge!

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:05.510
Spacious!

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:08.220
Well, would you look at that?

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:10.330
The room even has a bath attached to it!

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:14.370
A room like this has to cost a fortune!

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.670
I don't have that kind of money!

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:20.650
Would you calm yourself? 
Our accommodations have been arranged for.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:21.490
Really?

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:25.320
Indeed. We already had 
our tickets, didn't we?

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:26.890
You've got a point.

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:29.770
Hey! That's enough sulking, Sunao.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:32.050
You get to indulge a bit 
on someone else's coin.

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:33.730
Why not enjoy yourself?

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:39.750
Sorry... I was just thinking about 
what I'll say to Kotetsu tomorrow.

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:42.510
Just tell him how you really feel.

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:47.000
He's right. That's what Kotetsu 
would want to hear, as well.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:50.760
I've treated Kotetsu terribly all this time.

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:54.270
I want to give him a 
real apology tomorrow.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.010
I don't necessarily need 
to be in here, do I?

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:11.730
What're you on about? 
Don't waste an opportunity for mixed bathing.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:13.790
If you insist, Kiriha-sama...

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:20.790
Oh, come now. Someone's being bashful.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.470
Kiriha-san!

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:25.550
You really should make sure it's clean.

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:28.090
No telling what kind of 
use it might see tonight.

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:29.410
It won't be doing anything!

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:31.180
C-Cut it out!

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.440
Well, Sunao...

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.730
Do you want Kazuya to wash you?

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.450
What a feast!

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:50.510
Eat, now! Don't let an opportunity 
like this pass you by!

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:52.700
We should eat.

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:55.450
I'm not sure we can finish it all, though.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:58.190
Oh, that looks good, too!

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.210
Now, feed me!

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:00.410
Sheesh...

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:03.260
Kiriha-san, this isn't 
exactly good table manners.

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:08.410
How dare you feed me 
wasabi, you imbecile?!

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:10.470
You were literally asking for it!

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.940
That one next.

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:14.470
Come on, you can feed yourself.

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:17.150
This really is quite good!

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:24.730
You two sleep together?!

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:27.150
She always forces the issue...

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:29.990
What are you talking about? 
I know you love it.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:31.360
"Always"?

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:34.220
You just have no concept of restraint!

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:36.280
Less talk, more service!

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:38.750
Hey! Stop grinding on me!

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:39.420
There, there, there!

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:40.570
Kiriha-san!

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:42.250
What? Finally in the mood?

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:45.500
No! We should be more considerate.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:49.490
Sunao-san's sad because 
she can't see Kotetsu-kun.

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:53.490
I feel bad about the two of us getting 
along too well in front of her.

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:55.510
You don't understand a thing.

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:58.520
Sunao's mistaken about something.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:01.690
Even if she's able to 
see Kotetsu tomorrow,

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:04.310
I don't think she'll be able to 
bring him back as things stand.

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:06.020
But why?

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:10.030
Because she doesn't understand 
how Kotetsu feels.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:13.980
Kiriha-san, do you know why 
Kotetsu-kun isn't waking up?!

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:17.580
Of course. I'm a tsukumogami 
myself, you know.

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:20.700
I believe Honoka and Kukuri know, as well.

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:22.650
Then shouldn't somebody tell her?!

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:26.250
Imbecile. This isn't the kind of 
thing you can just explain away.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:29.930
But what if she doesn't catch on?

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:35.110
Which is why, in order to 
make her realize the truth...

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:36.310
Yeah?

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:38.620
We are going to continue to fool around!

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:40.060
But why?!

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:42.560
How do you like that, then?!

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:54.620
Kotetsu!

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:59.390
What's wrong, Kotetsu? 
Are you feeling sick?

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:05.580
Listen, there's something 
I really need to tell you.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:07.470
After everything I've done—

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:08.810
I'm sorry.

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:12.370
No! I'm the one who should apologize.

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:14.750
Ever since I was little, I always—

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:16.090
I'm so useless.

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:18.220
No! That was—

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:20.100
I'm the reason your brother died.

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:23.100
Listen to me! The truth is—

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:26.100
Because I'm just a tool.

00:08:29.090 --> 00:08:30.940
I'm sorry, Sunao-sama.

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:32.860
Kotetsu...

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:36.110
I can't stay with you anymore.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:37.370
Kotetsu!

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:24.040
<b>Tsugu</b>

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:24.040
<b>Tsugumomo</b>

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:23.510
<i>Tsugu Tsugumomo</i>!

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:28.540
<b>Tsugu</b>

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:28.540
<b>Tsugumomo</b>

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:28.540
<i>Tsugu Tsugumomo</i>.

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:34.550
It's farther away than I thought!

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:37.130
Kazuya, carry me.

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:40.800
You could just turn into an obi.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:44.510
Come on, you need to stay 
with us, or you'll get lost.

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:46.310
Spoilsport!

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:48.710
We're almost there.

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:59.820
This is the Cave of the Divine Navel?

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:05.420
Looks deep.

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:07.990
I can already feel the spiritual pressure.

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:14.050
Sunao-san, slow down! It's dangerous!

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:16.590
She's too tense...

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:35.110
It's huge!

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:40.740
The moss is glowing?

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:58.350
This must be the echo stone.

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:27.910
<i>Please wake up.</i>

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:46.180
Kotetsu!

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:47.430
Kotetsu!

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:55.940
Kotetsu, listen to me, please!

00:11:56.440 --> 00:12:00.940
I... I was always so mean to you!

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:06.950
I blamed you for my brother 
dying, called you a tool...

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:12.710
You're not waking up because 
you hate me, right?

00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:15.090
And that's fine...

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:21.080
You can find a partner who'll 
actually take good care of you!

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:25.970
Just... please wake up, Kotetsu!

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:31.580
Kotetsu...

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:42.630
They're amasogi!

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:46.990
Obi Jab!

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:54.750
They're after Kotetsu-kun?

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:56.750
Are these...

00:12:57.350 --> 00:13:00.250
The amasogi that Kotetsu 
and I exorcised?!

00:13:01.650 --> 00:13:04.510
If the echo stone created them...

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:06.760
then they're Kotetsu's feelings!

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:09.510
You could call them the 
manifestation of his self-doubt!

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:12.770
If they reach him, he's done for!

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:15.390
Keep calling out to Kotetsu, Sunao!

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:18.440
We'll occupy them in the meantime!

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:24.410
You have to give Kotetsu 
what he really wants!

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:27.860
Kotetsu! Kotetsu!

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:30.620
<i>What he really wants?</i>

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:34.790
<i>It's not an apology from me?</i>

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:40.670
There's no end to them!

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:42.170
Stay on your toes!

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:44.550
I don't understand...

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:46.680
Kotetsu.

00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:48.660
Kotetsu...

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:53.730
Kotetsu!

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:57.440
<i>I can hear Sunao-sama's voice.</i>

00:13:58.450 --> 00:14:03.190
<i>But I bet I'm just hearing 
it because I want to.</i>

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:06.910
<i>I was never any help to her.</i>

00:14:08.010 --> 00:14:10.380
<i>And I let Suou-sama die.</i>

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:16.200
<i>Even if I wake up, I know 
what Sunao-sama will say...</i>

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:18.710
<i>"I don't need you."</i>

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:21.730
You must be terrified of hearing those words.

00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:24.710
Suou-sama?

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:27.940
It's because I let you...

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:32.630
That's not what you need right now.

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:38.730
You're a sword. Fear and doubt 
will only dull your edge.

00:14:39.340 --> 00:14:43.470
You need to focus on what 
you want the most instead.

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:49.240
<i>What I want the most?</i>

00:14:58.270 --> 00:15:01.950
That's the aberration that 
killed Sunao's brother!

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:07.010
It's not like the weaklings 
we've been dealing with.

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:09.260
Be on your guard!

00:15:10.460 --> 00:15:11.260
Right!

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:25.150
Kazuya!

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:34.780
Stop!

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:38.790
Kotetsu!

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:42.140
You can't, Sunao-san!

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:43.450
Let go of me!

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:46.780
Kiriha-san, let's use Divine Possession!

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:48.550
We can't!

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:49.800
Why?!

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:54.300
If Divine Possession runs out before 
we can finish it off, we will all die!

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:55.640
But...

00:15:55.640 --> 00:16:00.870
This amasogi's strength is a reflection 
of the strength of Kotetsu's self-doubt.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:04.810
If Kotetsu won't wake up, I don't think...

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:09.070
Kotetsu!

00:16:15.190 --> 00:16:16.320
No...

00:16:19.210 --> 00:16:20.410
I...

00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:25.010
I wanted to apologize...

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:29.960
I just wanted him to live on...

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:35.970
<i>Sunao-sama is crying?</i>

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:37.970
<i>Please don't cry.</i>

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:41.860
<i>I want to protect her. To help her.</i>

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:45.300
<i>That's all I...</i>

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:48.230
<i>That's all I...</i>

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:53.740
<i>All I wanted...</i>

00:16:57.730 --> 00:16:58.490
No.

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:05.230
That's not all.

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:08.750
I finally understand.

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:10.260
I...

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:12.010
<i>I...</i>

00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:13.880
...want to be...

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:15.550
<i>...want to be...</i>

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:19.510
..with Sunao-sama!

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:19.510
...with Kotetsu!

00:17:35.290 --> 00:17:36.710
Kotetsu...

00:17:36.710 --> 00:17:39.660
I'm so sorry, Sunao-sama.

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:44.090
I... I thought you didn't 
want me anymore...

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:50.770
That you didn't need me anymore, 
and I was so scared!

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:54.640
Dummy! You should know better!

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:57.680
I'm the one who needs to apologize!

00:17:58.070 --> 00:18:00.690
Sunao-sama!

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:01.930
Kotetsu!

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:07.980
What a relief!

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:10.190
Would you stop bawling?

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:12.590
Wait, the amasogi—

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:20.820
That's...

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:27.390
Considering how connected 
they are, it's only natural.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:32.390
Divine Possession.

00:18:36.820 --> 00:18:41.670
Seriously, I am so glad that 
Kotetsu-kun made it back!

00:18:41.670 --> 00:18:46.100
This is tedious. How long do 
you intend to keep sobbing?

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:47.740
But...

00:18:47.740 --> 00:18:50.840
Look, the problem's been resolved.

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:53.110
We should take this night to relax.

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:55.780
Especially given the state she's in.

00:18:57.370 --> 00:18:59.110
What the heck is this?!

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:01.210
Sunao-sama!

00:19:01.210 --> 00:19:04.850
It's kind of like a side effect 
of the Divine Possession...

00:19:04.850 --> 00:19:06.240
A side effect?!

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:08.870
Wh-Wh-What's going to happen to her?!

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:14.030
Relax. She'll just be too 
exhausted to move for a night.

00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:17.290
Oh, no! Sunao-sama!

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:21.820
That being the case, 
make sure you take care of her.

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:30.620
I can't see a thing!

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:32.650
Why am I blindfolded?

00:19:33.850 --> 00:19:37.650
You've got to be kidding me...

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:42.390
Time to wash all the sweat, 
tears, and other miscellany away!

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:47.080
E-Excuse me, then...

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:48.550
Where are you touching?!

00:19:48.550 --> 00:19:50.660
I don't have an answer for that...

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:54.390
I-I'm so sorry! I really have no idea!

00:19:58.270 --> 00:20:00.800
I can't deal with this!

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:03.420
You'll have to help her with 
the toilet as well, mind you.

00:20:03.420 --> 00:20:05.930
Absolutely not!

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:08.930
<b>Some Days Later</b>

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:08.930
<b>Some Days Later</b>

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:08.930
Well, that's good to hear!

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:11.180
Thank you for everything.

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:15.190
Good to have ya back. Yes, indeedy.

00:20:17.100 --> 00:20:20.210
The thought of your 
wielder not wanting you

00:20:20.770 --> 00:20:23.850
is enough to cause this 
kind of commotion.

00:20:23.850 --> 00:20:27.460
Tsugumomo are quite fragile creatures.

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:28.950
Keep that in mind.

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:34.150
No need to worry. I want to be 
with you forever, Kiriha-san.

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:42.470
You even paid for our stay... 
I can't begin to thank you enough.

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:44.820
I paid for what, now?

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:45.990
Kukuri-sama.

00:20:46.990 --> 00:20:48.980
You have a guest.

00:20:48.980 --> 00:20:51.610
Well, that don't happen 
every day. For me?

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:52.350
Yes.

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:55.190
It's Kanayama Taguri-sama.

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:57.110
\h\h\hNeighbor Goddess\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
\h\hKanayama Taguri\h\h\h

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:57.110
Good afternoon.

00:20:57.460 --> 00:21:00.290
I've come for her, as promised.

00:21:00.290 --> 00:21:02.610
Wait, what promise is this?

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:04.780
Right. Take her away!

00:21:07.020 --> 00:21:08.620
Come along, now.

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:11.250
This will be fun.

00:21:13.150 --> 00:21:16.620
Why?! What the heck?!

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:17.630
Were our expenses paid by...

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:18.710
Correct.

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:22.630
Taguri paid for it all in exchange for 
Kukuri staying over for three days.

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:28.300
No!

00:21:26.150 --> 00:21:27.180
<i>And so,</i>

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:30.270
<i>by sacrificing Kukuri for three nights 
in exchange for travel and lodging,</i>

00:21:30.270 --> 00:21:32.390
<i>this case came to a close.</i>

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:35.640
<b>Little Girls Only</b>

00:21:33.050 --> 00:21:35.270
<i>What became of Kukuri while in</i>

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:50.030
Kanayama Shrine

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:38.320
<i>Taguri's clutches could only 
be described as tragic.</i>

00:21:38.320 --> 00:21:43.050
Now, Kukuri-chan, 
let's have lots of fun together...

00:21:44.220 --> 00:21:49.530
No!

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:33.010
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:20.820 --> 00:23:23.340
Four students have been involved 
with recent amasogi trouble.

00:23:23.340 --> 00:23:26.080
And they've been acting with an 
agenda in mind this entire time.

00:23:26.080 --> 00:23:27.710
What is at the core of 
this feud between the gods

00:23:27.710 --> 00:23:30.470
and tsukumogami that stretches 
back into the distant past?

00:23:30.470 --> 00:23:33.010
Next time on <i>Tsugu Tsugumomo</i>, 
Chapter 6: "The Lost Village."

00:23:30.470 --> 00:23:33.010
<b>The Lost Village</b>

00:23:33.010 --> 00:23:34.310
Don't miss it!

00:23:33.010 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>Don't miss it!</b>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.250
